  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 246 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nOur lull in precipitation chances will continue into the day \nMonday but our break is short-lived as shower and thunderstorm \npotential returns to northwest Iowa Monday night, and area-wide \nagain Tuesday into Wednesday. Given this will be another \nnorthwest flow regime, it's tough to get too involved in the \ndetails. That said, the Tuesday storms do seem to have a rather \nhealthy environment with increasing instability and modest deep \nlayer shear supportive of more organized convection. SPC does \nhave a day 4 15% risk for most of Iowa and WPC has put out a \nslight risk for excessive rainfall for Tuesday. The pattern \nremains relatively active through mid-week and then ridging \nbegins to build through the second half of this week.",
